1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,733
How does a breeze out at sea end up lighting your kitchen?

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,233
Let's follow the wind.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,133
Wind pushes on the long blades and turns the rotor.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,333
Inside the nacelle, a generator turns that spin into electricity.

5
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:18,933
A transformer steps the voltage up, so the power can travel across the grid with little loss, all the way to your home.

6
00:00:18,933 --> 00:00:25,000
A single large turbine can supply more than a thousand homes, a rough but commonly cited figure.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,900
And the wind keeps working after dark, often blowing hardest at night, when solar panels are resting.

8
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,400
Every clip in this video came from one short GPU session.

9
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:35,933
Made with Comfyrizz.
